[# features/icon-text: an icon on the left with a title and short description on the right, on one row.

   Two table cells: the icon (a plain img with explicit size) and the text. Good for lists of benefits.
   The icon is decorative by default (alt is empty) because the title says the same thing.

   Compatibility
   - Outlook desktop: table cells and images honored.
   - Gmail apps: fine. The two cells stay side by side on phones, keep the text short.
   - Dark mode: text swaps via dm-text and dm-muted where prefers-color-scheme is honored. Icons are not recolored. #]
<mj-text[[ cc(cls) ]] align="left" padding="[[ s.padding ]]">
  <table role="presentation" width="100%" border="0" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0"><tr>
    <td width="[[ s.iconSize | replace('px', '') | int + (s.gap | replace('px', '') | int) ]]" valign="[[ s.valign ]]" style="width:[[ s.iconSize | replace('px', '') | int + (s.gap | replace('px', '') | int) ]]px;padding-right:[[ s.gap ]];">
      <img src="[[ data.icon.src ]]" alt="[[ data.icon.alt ]]" width="[[ s.iconSize | replace('px', '') ]]" height="[[ s.iconSize | replace('px', '') ]]" style="display:block;border:0;width:[[ s.iconSize ]];height:[[ s.iconSize ]];border-radius:[[ s.iconRadius ]];">
    </td>
    <td valign="[[ s.valign ]]">
      <div class="dm-text" style="[[ typoCss('h4') ]]padding-bottom:2px;">[[ data.title ]]</div>
      [% if data.description %]<div class="dm-muted" style="[[ typoCss('bodySmall', { color: 'mutedText' }) ]]">[[ data.description ]]</div>[% endif %]
    </td>
  </tr></table>
</mj-text>
